83             3) REQUIRED - Key user settings (libraries, data sets, variables and box plot options)
84                M_LB:   Libname containing ADaM measurement data, such as ADVS.
85                        WORK by default, since step (2) creates the desired WORK subset.
86                M_DS:   Measuments data set, such as ADVS.
87         
88                T_VAR:  Variable in M_DS with the Treatment Name, such as TRTP, TRTA.
89                TN_VAR: Variable in M_DS with the Treatment Number (display controls order), such as TRTPN, TRTAN.
90                M_VAR:  Variable in M_DS with measurements data, such as AVAL.
91                LO_VAR: Variable in M_DS with LOWER LIMIT of reference range, such as ANRLO.
92                        Required to highlight values outside reference range (RED DOT in box plot), and reference lines
93                HI_VAR: Variable in M_DS with UPPER LIMIT of reference range, such as ANRHI.
94                        Required to highlight values outside reference range (RED DOT in box plot), and reference lines
95         
96                P_FL:  Population flag variable. 'Y' indicates record is in population of interest.
97                A_FL:  Analysis Flag variable.   'Y' indicates that record is selected for analysis.
98         
99                REF_LINES:
100                     Option to specify which Normal Range reference lines to include in box plots
101                     <NONE | UNIFORM | NARROW | ALL | numeric-value(s)> See discussion in Central Tendency White Paper
102                     NONE    - No reference lines on box plot
103                     UNIFORM - Default. preferred alternative to default. Only plot LOW/HIGH ref lines if uniform for all obs
104                     NARROW  - Display only the narrow normal limits: max LOW, and min HIGH limits
105                     ALL     - Discouraged, since displaying ALL reference lines confuses review of data display
106                     numeric-values - space-delimited list of reference line values, such as a 0 reference line for displays of
106      ! change.
107        
108               MAX_BOXES_PER_PAGE:
109                     Maximum number of boxes to display per plot page (see "Notes", above)
110        
111               OUTPUTS_FOLDER:
